  "case_id": "c51_neighbor_info_at_the_receipts_own_instant",
  "title": "A NeighborInfo report sent at the receipt's own instant is in the 24-hour window",
  "rules": ["lnk_01", "lnk_02", "lnk_04", "lnk_05"],
  "reasoning": [
    "Casey's Q2 answer (PR #66 comment 6968763406, item 2), as PR #67 words it in lnk_01: \"Both edges of the 24 hours count: a delivery exactly 24 hours before the receipt, and one at the receipt's own instant, are in the window, for candidates and for NeighborInfo reports alike\".",
    "The receipts come from c51-s (byte 80) at c51-g with relay 97, so none is a direct hop. c51-g's only NeighborInfo report was sent at 23 10:10:00 and lists one neighbour, c51-r (byte 97). By radio c51-g heard only its own packets and c51-s, so no candidate has 97 and relay_node never resolves (lnk_01).",
    "10:10:00: the report was sent at the receipt's own instant, so it is in the window and lists exactly one neighbour with 97: relayer c51-r, link_source neighbor_info. 10:20 and 10:30: the same report, 10 and 20 minutes before, resolves them the same way.",
    "c51-r is stationary on c20 and c51-g on g16 (lnk_02), and every receipt passes lnk_05 at 2745.603 m, so all three are counted. 3 packets: kept. An implementation that leaves the receipt's own instant out of the window drops the 10:10 receipt by lnk_01, and the hour, with 2 packets, by lnk_04.",
    "Medians: SNR 5, 6 and 7 dB give 6.0; RSSI -90, -95 and -100 dBm give -95.0. position_uncertainty_m is c20 22.734410 m plus g16 363.750397 m, = 386.484807 m (lnk_05). Neither end is precise: both were sent on the public broker only."
  ],
